@bank all
// SW3 (2026-10-26, Pillar 5 Step 5, S5-4): the crew around your shutdowns. Bubbles, 60 characters.
// sd.warned: a person you warned from the screen or in person (their answer).
// sd.off: someone in a fed room when the power goes off at the booked hour.
// sd.thanks: the next day or after, someone whose room was off and who was warned (a quiet hour).
// sd.grumble: the same, when the hour clashed with a meal, a class or a tradition, or they weren't told.
// sd.lapsed: the day after a missed hour (they moved their day for nothing).
== sd.warned
- Tomorrow? Thanks for saying. I'll plan round it.
- An hour off? Fine. I'll go somewhere else.
- Good of you to tell me. Most just switch it off.
- Noted. Thanks. I'll save my work first.

== sd.off
- Lights. Right. That's the shutdown, then.
- There it goes. Right on time.
- I was warned. I was warned. Still made me jump.   #funny
- Power's off in here. Tea break, then.   #funny

== sd.thanks
- Thanks for warning us about the power. Very tidy.
- That shutdown? Didn't even notice. That's good, isn't it?
- You picked a quiet hour. Thank you for that.

== sd.grumble
- Power off at mealtime? Really? I was hungry.
- Nobody told me about the power. I was mid-wash.
- The gym class moved for your shutdown. Twice the stairs.   #funny
- Next time, maybe not right in the middle of dinner?
- A shutdown at the quiz? I had the answer to number six.   #funny

== sd.lapsed
- We moved our whole morning for that shutdown. It never came.
- Was the power going off or not? We waited.
